// Regression: do[List] with >=2 bindings followed by a closure that declares
// a local variable whose name shadows one of the do-binding variables caused an
// ICE at BytecodeGeneration (Index -1 out of bounds for length 0 in
// ClosureCodegen.emitNewClosure). Root cause: CapturedVariableScanner did not
// track locally-declared names and wrongly treated them as method-level captures
// that needed boxing. The boxed flag then made the codegen try to loadLocal using
// a JVM-slot value as a newLocal index, which is invalid.
def main(): void {
  val data: List[Object] = do[List] {
    x <- [1, 2]
    y <- [3, 4]
    ret [x, y]
  }
  val r = data.filter { pair ->
    val x = (pair as List[Object])[0] as Int
    x > 1
  }
  IO::println(r.toString())
}
